## What the RES is

The Real Estate Scheme is, in the words of the Economic Development Board, another of the luxury residential offerings of Mauritius: villas, penthouses, duplexes and apartments in exclusive but smaller developments. Foreigners can buy in **existing RES projects**.

## Residency and rights

A purchase of **USD 375,000 or more** gives the buyer and dependants a residence permit. Owners may rent the property, become tax resident and repatriate the money from a sale or from rent without restriction, and they do not need an occupation or work permit to invest and work in Mauritius.

## Costs on top of the price

- **First purchase** from the RES company: registration duty of USD 70,000 or 5% of the price, whichever is lower.
- **Resale**: 5% registration duty for the buyer, 5% land transfer tax for the seller.
- **EDB processing fee**: MUR 25,000 per application.

## The RES on the west coast

The EDB publishes a list of RES projects. On the list dated November 2022, **22 of the 77 projects** are on our stretch of coast: 15 in [Tamarin](/en/areas/tamarin) (including La Mivoie and Plantation Marguery), 6 in [Black River](/en/areas/black-river) (including La Preneuse and Cascavelle) and 1 in [Chamarel](/en/areas/chamarel). Most of the others are in the north, around Grand Baie and Pereybère. The list is a few years old, so ask any developer for its current RES certificate.

## Paying, renting and selling

The same rules apply as under the [PDS](/en/living-in-the-west/pds): money from abroad, staged payments off plan, letting through the developer or its manager, and 30 days' notice to the EDB before a sale.

*Rules and amounts change. Everything here was checked against the Economic Development Board's own pages on 2 October 2026; confirm the details with the EDB, your notary and the developer before you sign.*
